dialogue dorrit
  node root dorrit "Ah. A colleague. Customs, twenty-two years, then the sea, for my nerves. Nothing leaves this galley uninspected, clerk. Not a biscuit."
    > "Then why isn't dinner served?" -> stamp
    > "You must miss it. Customs." -> miss
    > "Good day, Mr Dorrit." -> bye
  node stamp dorrit "The stew has not been passed. I have no stamp. I left it in Port Vela with my pension."
    > "Couldn't you just… serve it?" -> serve
    > "I have a harbour stamp." if has stamp -> harbour
  node serve dorrit "Unpassed? I have seen what unpassed food does to a crew, clerk. I have seen what it did to a herring."
    > "I have a harbour stamp." if has stamp -> harbour
    > "Good day." -> bye
  node harbour dorrit "A harbour stamp. Aboard. In a galley. …Then why are we talking? The pot is on the stove, man. Regulation ink only."
  node miss dorrit "Every day. The sea has no forms, clerk. Things simply happen out here, unrecorded, one after another. It's barbaric."
    > "Then why isn't dinner served?" -> stamp
    > "Good day." -> bye
  node bye dorrit "Good day. Wipe your feet. Both of them. I'll be checking."
  # Stamping the stew (rooms.ts, below_decks).
  node passed dorrit "PASSED FOR CONSUMPTION. In purple. On a potato. …Beautiful. Regulation ink."
    > "You're welcome." -> gong
      set dinner
      sound chime
    > "I've stamped worse. Never better." -> gong
      set dinner
      sound chime
  node gong narrator "He strikes the gong. The whole ship arrives at once, Hobb first, and the bosun's place by Pell's chest is suddenly very empty."
  node fed dorrit "Seconds are available on application. Thirds require a countersignature."
    > "Where did you learn to cook?" -> cook
    > "Thank you, Mr Dorrit." -> welcome
  node cook dorrit "I didn't. I learned to inspect. The stew simply knows it's being watched."
  node welcome dorrit "Thank the stamp. I merely recognised its authority."
